        "# Sensitivity Analysis: When Does the Graph Help?\n",
        "**MSP470S project, notebook 4 of 4**\n",
        "\n",
        "| | |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| **Project title** | Talent Matching: A Graph Neural Network Recommender for Ranking Candidate–Employer Matches |\n",
        "| **Author** | Luyolo Sokatsha (student number 217148875) |\n",
        "| **Module** | MSP470S Mathematical Sciences Project 4 |\n",
        "| **Qualification** | Advanced Diploma in Mathematical Sciences |\n",
        "| **Institution** | Cape Peninsula University of Technology (CPUT) |\n",
        "| **Date** | November 2026 |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Project in one paragraph\n",
        "Talent-matching platforms must decide which employers to show each candidate first. This project compares a graph neural network (GNN) with simpler recommenders (popularity, BPR matrix factorisation, logistic regression) on **fully synthetic** candidate–employer data, using a time-based test, Recall@K and NDCG@K, an ablation, a cold-start test and a sensitivity analysis. No real people, companies or confidential records are used.\n",
        "\n",
        "## What this notebook does\n",
        "Repeats the whole model comparison in six synthetic worlds that differ in the strength of the hidden collaborative signal (0.35, 1.0, 2.0) and in the number of contacts per candidate (12 or 30), with a lighter tuning search and three seeds per world. The notebook writes the generator (`gen_core.py`) and the model script (`msp470s_models.py`) to your working folder and runs the script once per world. It then draws the summary figure and the shortfall table (how far each model is behind the best model in each world).\n",
        "\n",
        "| | |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| **Needs** | Nothing from the other notebooks (it generates its own data). |\n",
        "| **Produces** | `results_sensitivity/` (one folder per world, `sensitivity_summary.csv`, `regret_table.csv`, `fig_sensitivity.png`) |\n",
        "| **Run time** | About 25 minutes on a CPU for all six worlds (set `QUICK = True` for a 3-minute test) |\n",
        "\n",
        "## How to run\n",
        "1. In Google Colab choose **Runtime → Run all** (or run the cells from top to bottom). A GPU is not required.\n",
        "2. The setup cell can mount your Google Drive so that all files are kept between sessions in the folder `MyDrive/MSP470S_Project`. Set `USE_DRIVE = False` to work in temporary Colab storage instead.\n",
        "3. Run the four notebooks in order: 01 → 02 → 03 → 04 (04 is optional and slow)."
      ]
